          "bbox": [
            0.161,
            0.673,
            0.845,
            0.713
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Draw the initial few steps (at least till Step 2) of the shape sequence that leads to the Sierpinski Triangle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.721,
            0.846,
            0.762
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Find the number of holes, and the triangles that remain at each step of the shape sequence that leads to the Sierpinski Triangle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.768,
            0.848,
            0.828
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Find the area of the region remaining at the nth step in each of the shape sequences that lead to the Sierpinski fractals. Take the area of the starting square/triangle to be 1 sq. unit."
